(Python emphasizes readability. Unlike many languages, Python uses indentation to define blocks of code. Consistent indentation) Tj
T* (is therefore part of Python's syntax. The indented print\(\) statement belongs to the if block. Four spaces are commonly used for) Tj
T* (one indentation level. Important: Mixing tabs and spaces inconsistently can cause indentation errors. Use a consistent) Tj
T* (indentation style.) Tj
