(Variables and data types are fundamental concepts in Python programming. A variable is a name that refers to a value or object) Tj
T* (stored in memory. Variables allow us to store information and use that information later in a program. A data type tells us what) Tj
T* (kind of value an object represents and what operations can be performed with that value. Python is dynamically typed, which) Tj
T* (means you do not have to explicitly declare the type of a variable before assigning a value to it. The same variable name can) Tj
T* (refer to objects of different types at different times.) Tj
