(A variable is a name that is bound to an object. When you assign 'age = 25', 'age' is the variable name, '=' is the assignment) Tj
T* (operator, and '25' is an integer object stored in memory. The basic syntax is 'variable_name = value'. Python evaluates the value) Tj
T* (on the right side and assigns the resulting object to the name on the left side. Multiple variables can be assigned in one) Tj
T* (statement: 'a, b, c = 10, 20, 30'. You can also assign the same object to multiple names simultaneously: 'x = y = z = 100'.) Tj
