(Operators and expressions are fundamental building blocks of Python programs. An operator is a symbol or keyword that tells) Tj
T* (Python to perform an operation. An operand is a value or object on which an operator performs an operation. An expression is a) Tj
T* (combination of values, variables, operators, function calls, or other elements that Python can evaluate to produce a value. For) Tj
T* (example: a = 10 b = 20 result = a + b Here: - a and b are operands. - + is an operator. - a + b is an expression. - 30 is the value) Tj
T* (produced by the expression. Operators allow us to perform essential tasks such as: - Mathematical calculations - Comparing) Tj
T* (values - Assigning and updating values - Performing logical decision-making - Working with binary bits - Checking membership) Tj
T* (within sequences and mappings - Comparing object memory identity) Tj
