(Logical operators combine or modify Boolean conditions: - and: True only when BOTH operands are true. - or: True when AT) Tj
T* (LEAST ONE operand is true. - not: Unary operator that reverses the Boolean state \(not True -> False\). Short-Circuit Evaluation:) Tj
T* (Python evaluates logical expressions lazily from left to right: - In 'False and func\(\)', because the first operand is False, Python) Tj
T* (stops immediately and never invokes func\(\). - In 'True or func\(\)', because the first operand is True, Python stops immediately and) Tj
T* (never invokes func\(\). Truth Value Testing \(Truthy and Falsy\): Any Python object can be tested for its Boolean truth value using) Tj
T* (bool\(\). The following values evaluate to False: False, None, 0, 0.0, empty strings \(""\), empty lists \([]\), empty tuples \(\(\)\), empty) Tj
T* (dictionaries \({}\), empty sets \(set\(\)\). Most other objects evaluate to True \(e.g. bool\("Python"\) is True, bool\([1, 2, 3]\) is True\).) Tj
