(Membership operators test whether a value is contained inside a collection \(list, tuple, string, set, or dictionary\): - 'in': Returns) Tj
T* (True if the specified item exists in the collection. fruits = ["apple", "banana", "orange"] "apple" in fruits # True "Python" in "Python) Tj
T* (Programming" # True - 'not in': Returns True if the item is absent. names = ["Rahul", "Arun", "Priya"] "John" not in names # True -) Tj
T* (Membership in Dictionaries: When used directly on a dictionary, membership tests check the dictionary's KEYS, not its values:) Tj
T* (student = {"name": "Rahul", "age": 21} "name" in student # True \(checks if "name" is a key\) "Rahul" in student # False \(checks) Tj
T* (keys, not values\)) Tj
