(Identity operators test whether two references point to the exact same object in computer memory: - 'is': True if both variables) Tj
T* (refer to the identical object in RAM \(id\(a\) == id\(b\)\). - 'is not': True if both variables refer to distinct objects. CRITICAL) Tj
T* (DISTINCTION: == vs is - '==' compares VALUES \(content equality: do they contain the same data?\). - 'is' checks OBJECT) Tj
T* (IDENTITY \(are they the same object in RAM?\). Example: a = [1, 2, 3] b = [1, 2, 3] a == b # True \(contents match\) a is b # False) Tj
T* (\(two distinct list instances in memory\) Best Practice: Always use 'is' when checking for None: if result is None: print\("No result"\)) Tj
