(52 to 58. Operator Precedence & Associativity \(PEMDAS Rules\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
42.5196850393700814 671.8112598425196893 Td
(When an expression contains multiple operators, Python follows defined precedence rules to determine evaluation order:) Tj
T* (Parentheses have the highest priority and override default precedence: result = 10 + 5 * 2 # 10 + 10 = 20 \(Multiplication before) Tj
T* (Addition\) result = \(10 + 5\) * 2 # 15 * 2 = 30 \(Parentheses override precedence\) Operator Associativity: - Most operators evaluate) Tj
T* (from Left to Right: 20 - 5 - 3 = \(20 - 5\) - 3 = 12 - Exponentiation \(**\) evaluates from Right to Left: 2 ** 3 ** 2 = 2 ** \(3 ** 2\) = 2 ** 9) Tj
T* (= 512 \(NOT \(2 ** 3\) ** 2 = 64\)) Tj
