(A condition can use a value directly. Python treats some values as false \(falsy\) and most other values as true \(truthy\). Common) Tj
T* (Falsy Values in Python: - False - None - Numeric zero \(0, 0.0\) - Empty strings \(""\) - Empty containers such as [], \(\), {}, and set\(\)) Tj
T* (Practical Pythonic Check: name = "" if name: print\("A name was entered."\) else: print\("The name is empty."\) An empty string is) Tj
T* (falsy, so the program prints that the name is empty. Checking a list directly is also useful: 'if items:' means the list has at least) Tj
T* (one element.) Tj
