(- The if Statement: Runs a block only when its condition is true. The colon \(:\) starts the block, and consistent 4-space indentation) Tj
T* (defines which statements belong to it. - Adding else: Provides an alternative branch when the condition is false: number = 7 if) Tj
T* (number % 2 == 0: print\("The number is even."\) else: print\("The number is odd."\) - Using elif for Multiple Choices: Python checks) Tj
T* (from top to bottom, runs the first matching block, and skips the remaining branches. Order matters: always put the highest or) Tj
T* (most specific condition first! - Nested Conditionals vs Combined Conditions: A nested conditional is an if statement inside) Tj
T* (another conditional block: age = 20 has_id = True if age >= 18: if has_id: print\("Entry approved."\) else: print\("Please show) Tj
T* (identification."\) else: print\("You must be at least 18."\) Sometimes a logical expression is simpler than nesting: if age >= 18 and) Tj
T* (has_id: print\("Entry approved."\) else: print\("Entry requirements were not met."\) Use nesting when the second decision only) Tj
T* (matters after the first; combine conditions when they form one unified rule.) Tj
