(An exception is an error or unexpected event raised while a program runs \(e.g. converting non-numeric text to an integer,) Tj
T* (dividing by zero, or accessing missing keys\). An unhandled exception terminates the program abruptly. Core Exception Handling) Tj
T* (Mechanics: - try: The code that might raise an error goes here. - except SpecificError: Catches and handles expected exceptions) Tj
T* (\(e.g. ValueError, ZeroDivisionError\). - else: Optional clause that runs ONLY when the try block completes successfully without) Tj
T* (any exception. - except SpecificError as error: Captures the exception object to inspect its diagnostic message. - finally: Optional) Tj
T* (block that executes unconditionally whether or not an exception occurred, ideal for cleanup. Best Practice: Always catch specific) Tj
T* (exceptions! Avoid a bare 'except:' that catches everything; it can hide programming mistakes, typos, and syntax errors, making) Tj
T* (debugging difficult.) Tj
