(Iteration means repeating a set of instructions. Each single pass through the loop body is called an iteration. A loop avoids) Tj
T* (repetitive code: instead of writing print\("Hello"\) three times, a loop executes the same statement with clean, concise syntax: for _) Tj
T* (in range\(3\): print\("Hello"\) Python provides two primary loop statements: - The while loop: Repeats statements as long as an) Tj
T* (underlying condition remains True \(indefinite iteration\). - The for loop: Iterates over each item in a collection or sequence, such) Tj
T* (as a list, string, or range \(definite iteration\). Rule of thumb: Choose while when repetition depends on a dynamic condition or) Tj
T* (user input. Choose for when iterating over known collections or repeating a fixed number of times.) Tj
ET
