T* (\(e.g., smallest = numbers[0]\), NOT arbitrary values like 0. Initializing to 0 fails for all-negative or all-positive lists! - Empty) Tj
T* (Collection Guard: Check 'if numbers:' before indexing numbers[0] to prevent IndexError, or use Python's built-in min\(numbers,) Tj
T* (default=None\). - enumerate\(iterable, start=0\): Provides both the index and value simultaneously without manual counters \(e.g.,) Tj
T* ('for idx, item in enumerate\(fruits\):'\). - Nested Loops: A loop inside another loop. The inner loop completes all its iterations for) Tj
T* (every single iteration of the outer loop \(useful for grids, tables, and permutations\). - Loop else Clause: A for or while loop can) Tj
T* (have an else block. The loop's else executes ONLY when the loop finishes normally without hitting a break statement \(invaluable) Tj
T* (for search loops\).) Tj
