(Python provides flexible ways to pass arguments to functions: 1. Positional Arguments: Matched to parameters strictly by) Tj
T* (position/order from left to right. add\(4, 7\) assigns 4 to 'first' and 7 to 'second'. 2. Keyword Arguments: You explicitly name the) Tj
T* (parameter in the call \(e.g., describe_pet\(animal="dog", name="Rex"\)\). Keyword arguments can be provided in any order and) Tj
T* (greatly improve code readability when functions take multiple configuration options. 3. Default Arguments: Allow parameters to) Tj
T* (have fallback default values if the caller omits them \(e.g. def describe_pet\(animal, name="Milo"\):\). CRITICAL RULE: In a function) Tj
T* (definition, all required parameters must appear before parameters with default values. Defining def func\(a=1, b\): causes a) Tj
T* (SyntaxError!) Tj
