(Complete the following 8 practical Python data structure programs: Program 1: Word Frequency Histogram & Top-K Counter Given a) Tj
T* (sentence, count word frequencies using a dictionary and extract the top 3 most frequent words using Counter. Program 2: 2D Grid) Tj
T* (Transposition Given a 3x3 matrix of numbers, use nested list comprehensions to compute its transpose \(swap rows and columns\).) Tj
T* (Program 3: Dictionary Inverter with Duplicate Value Grouping Invert a dictionary mapping student names to grades so that each grade) Tj
T* (maps to a list of student names. Program 4: DSU Multi-Field Sorter Given a list of words, use the Decorate-Sort-Undecorate \(DSU\)) Tj
T* (pattern to sort words primarily by length \(ascending\) and secondarily alphabetically \(case-insensitive\). Program 5: Configuration Merger) Tj
T* (with Union Operator Given default app settings and user custom overrides, merge them using the Python 3.9+ union operator \(|\) and) Tj
T* (print the active configuration. Program 6: Sales Record Grouping with setdefault\(\) Given a list of sales transactions \(category, amount\),) Tj
T* (group the transactions by category and calculate total sales per category. Program 7: Role-Based Access Control \(RBAC\) with Sets) Tj
T* (Given a set of user permissions and required endpoint permissions, compute missing permissions and determine if access is granted) Tj
T* (using set difference and subset operations. Program 8: Sliding Window Rate Limiter with deque Implement a sliding-window timestamp) Tj
T* (tracker using collections.deque that records request timestamps and rejects requests exceeding 3 actions within a 10-second window.) Tj
