(Strings are among the most versatile and ubiquitous data structures in Python programming. A string is an immutable, ordered) Tj
T* (sequence of characters representing textual data. From parsing server logs and extracting API parameters to validating email) Tj
T* (addresses and generating formatted invoices, text processing is a core pillar of software development. In Python, every) Tj
T* (character in a string is represented internally using Unicode \(UTF-8 by default\), allowing programs to manipulate characters,) Tj
T* (symbols, and emojis across all written languages seamlessly. Because strings are sequences, they share fundamental behaviors) Tj
T* (with lists and tuples - such as zero-based indexing, slicing, iteration, and membership testing - while enforcing strict immutability.) Tj
T* (This comprehensive module covers the full anatomy of Python strings: character indexing, step-based slicing, immutability and) Tj
T* (memory interning, frequency analysis, case normalization, searching and validation methods, delimiter tokenization with split\(\)) Tj
T* (and join\(\), regex-free text extraction patterns, modern f-string interpolation, computational complexity, and 8 real-world practice) Tj
T* (programs.) Tj
