(A string in Python is an ordered sequence of characters enclosed in single quotes \('...'\), double quotes \("..."\), or triple quotes) Tj
T* (\('''...''' or """..."""\). Indexing Principles: Each character has a fixed numeric index: - Positive indexing starts at 0 for the first) Tj
T* (character and proceeds to len\(s\) - 1. - Negative indexing starts at -1 for the last character and counts backwards to -len\(s\).) Tj
T* (Boundary Errors: Attempting to access an index beyond the valid range \(e.g. s[len\(s\)]\) raises an IndexError: string index out of) Tj
T* (range. Character Encoding with ord\(\) and chr\(\): Under the hood, every character corresponds to an integer code point: - ord\('A'\)) Tj
T* (returns 65 \(ASCII / Unicode decimal value\). - chr\(65\) returns 'A'. - ord\('a'\) returns 97 \(lowercase letters have higher numeric code) Tj
T* (points than uppercase\). - ord\('EUR'\) returns 8364 \(full Unicode international character support\).) Tj
