(When you call Python's built-in open\(\) function, Python does not instantly read the entire file into RAM. Instead, it asks the host) Tj
T* (operating system \(Windows, Linux, or macOS\) to locate the file on disk, verify permissions, and return a stream pointer called a) Tj
T* ('File Handle'. Syntax: file_handle = open\(filename, mode='r', encoding='utf-8'\) Key Components of a File Handle: - File Cursor:) Tj
T* (An internal pointer tracking the exact byte position where the next read or write operation will begin. - I/O Buffer: A small chunk of) Tj
T* (memory managed by the OS that batches disk reads and writes for high performance. - Encoding Translator: Decodes raw) Tj
T* (binary bytes from disk into human-readable Unicode Python string objects. If Python successfully finds and opens the file, it) Tj
T* (returns a _io.TextIOWrapper object. If the file cannot be found in the specified path, Python halts execution and raises a) Tj
T* (FileNotFoundError.) Tj
