BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
42.5196850393700814 517.6065354330708033 Td
(A core workload in backend engineering is parsing server telemetry and email mailboxes. The Unix MBOX format stores) Tj
T* (thousands of messages in a single continuous text file where each new message begins with the prefix 'From '. Pattern 1: The) Tj
T* ('StartsWith' Filter Process only lines that start with a specific header prefix: for line in fhand: line = line.rstrip\(\) if) Tj
T* (line.startswith\('From:'\): print\(line\) Pattern 2: The 'Skip Uninteresting Lines' \(continue\) Pattern Writing deeply nested if blocks) Tj
T* (makes code unreadable. In production, flip the logic to skip lines immediately using continue: for line in fhand: line = line.rstrip\(\) if) Tj
T* (not line.startswith\('From:'\): continue # Process interesting lines cleanly at top indentation level pieces = line.split\(\) email =) Tj
T* (pieces[1] print\(email\) Pattern 3: Header Extraction & Conversion Searching for floating-point metrics \(e.g. spam confidence) Tj
T* (headers in email servers\): # Line format: 'X-DSPAM-Confidence: 0.8475' for line in fhand: if) Tj
T* (line.startswith\('X-DSPAM-Confidence:'\): col_pos = line.find\(':'\) num_str = line[col_pos + 1:].strip\(\) confidence = float\(num_str\)) Tj
