(Real-world file systems are unpredictable: disks fill up, users provide invalid file names, files are locked by other processes, or) Tj
T* (network shares disconnect. Production software must catch expected I/O exceptions gracefully: 1. FileNotFoundError: Raised) Tj
T* (when the target file path cannot be resolved. Always prompt the user or fall back to sensible defaults. 2. PermissionError: Raised) Tj
T* (when the operating system denies access \(e.g. attempting to write to a read-only directory or read a file owned by) Tj
T* (root/administrator\). 3. UnicodeDecodeError: Raised when a file encoded in Latin-1 or Shift-JIS contains byte sequences that are) Tj
T* (invalid under the requested UTF-8 decoder. Handled by verifying encoding or using errors='replace'. 4. IsADirectoryError: Raised) Tj
T* (when code attempts to open a folder path as if it were a text file.) Tj
