(When hunting a logic flaw across a 1,000-line script or a large pipeline: The Inefficient Approach \(Linear Search\): Reading) Tj
T* (line-by-line from line 1 to line 1,000 requires O\(N\) effort and is mentally exhausting. The Scientific Bisection Strategy \(Binary) Tj
T* (Search\): 1. Place a diagnostic breakpoint or logging probe at the midpoint \(Line 500\). 2. Inspect whether the program state \(all) Tj
T* (variables and data structures\) is 100% correct at line 500: - If State is VALID at Line 500: The bug CANNOT be in lines 1 - 500! It) Tj
T* (must reside in lines 501 - 1000. - If State is CORRUPTED at Line 500: The bug has ALREADY occurred! It must reside in lines 1) Tj
T* (- 500. 3. Bisect the remaining half by testing line 250 or line 750. 4. Mathematical Efficiency: In a 1,000-line program, bisection) Tj
T* (isolates the exact defective line in approximately log2\(1000\) ~= 10 checks!) Tj
