(Defensive programming involves embedding self-checks into code to detect internal inconsistencies as early as possible. The) Tj
T* (assert Statement: Syntax: assert <condition>, <error_message> If the condition evaluates to True, nothing happens. If it) Tj
T* (evaluates to False, Python immediately raises an AssertionError: def calculate_discount\(price, discount_percent\): assert price >=) Tj
T* (0, f"Price cannot be negative: {price}" assert 0 <= discount_percent <= 100, f"Discount must be 0-100%: {discount_percent}") Tj
T* (return price * \(1 - discount_percent / 100\) CRITICAL Production Warning Regarding assert: Python disables assertions when) Tj
T* (executed with the -O \(optimize\) flag \(python -O app.py\). Therefore, NEVER use assert for security checks, user input validation,) Tj
T* (or business logic enforcement! Use regular if statements and raise ValueError\(...\) instead.) Tj
