(Complete the following 8 comprehensive hands-on exception handling and debugging challenges: 1. Resilient Numerical Parser with) Tj
T* (Type Validation: Write a function safe_parse_int_list\(string_values\) that accepts a list of string representations, converts them to) Tj
T* (integers, logs warnings for unparseable items without halting, and returns a tuple of \(valid_integers, error_count\). 2. Safe Configuration) Tj
T* (File Loader with Schema Validation: Create a function load_validated_config\(filepath\) that reads a key-value text file. Raise a custom) Tj
T* (MissingConfigKeyError if mandatory keys \('DATABASE_HOST', 'API_KEY'\) are absent, and catch FileNotFoundError gracefully with) Tj
T* (default settings fallback. 3. Complete E-Commerce Transaction Guard \(try/except/else/finally\): Implement a process_payment\(account,) Tj
T* (amount\) function simulating a payment gateway. Demonstrate the execution of all four blocks: try \(charge\), except \(InsufficientFunds,) Tj
T* (InvalidCard\), else \(send receipt\), and finally \(audit logging\). 4. Custom Banking Exception Hierarchy with Account Lockout: Create an) Tj
T* (exception hierarchy rooted at BankAccountError. Implement InsufficientFundsError and AccountSuspendedError. Write an account debit) Tj
T* (method that raises these exceptions and tracks failed attempts to lock accounts after 3 consecutive errors. 5. Chained Exception) Tj
T* (Translator \(API Adapter Pattern\): Simulate an external HTTP API client that catches low-level socket and timeout exceptions \(simulate) Tj
T* (with ConnectionRefusedError\) and re-raises an ApplicationGatewayError using the 'raise ... from' syntax. 6. Scientific Bisection Defect) Tj
T* (Hunter: Given a list of 1,000 processed transaction records where exactly one record contains corrupted non-numerical data causing a) Tj
T* (calculation function to crash, implement a binary search bisection algorithm that locates the exact defective index in <= 10 steps. 7.) Tj
T* (Production Logging & Audit Recorder: Build a module that configures a rotating memory logger. Record DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, and) Tj
T* (ERROR events across a simulated user login workflow, and extract all ERROR logs into a separate security incident summary. 8.) Tj
T* (Automated Retry Strategy with Jitter & Max Attempt Guard: Write a decorator or higher-order function with_retry\(max_attempts,) Tj
T* (allowed_exceptions\) that retries transient operations \(e.g. database locks or network timeouts\) with exponential backoff before finally) Tj
T* (raising a MaxRetriesExceededError.) Tj
