(One of the most distinctive features of Python OOP is the mandatory first parameter self in all instance methods. What is self?) Tj
T* (self represents the specific object instance currently executing the method. When you invoke a method on an object: s.party\(\)) Tj
T* (Python automatically converts that call behind the scenes into: PartyAnimal.party\(s\) Why self is Explicit: Unlike C++ or Java) Tj
T* (\(which use an implicit 'this' pointer\), Python follows the Zen of Python maxim: 'Explicit is better than implicit.' By receiving self) Tj
T* (explicitly, method bodies can unambiguously access and modify the invoking object's private namespace: self.points += 1 #) Tj
T* (Mutates the calling object's points attribute only!) Tj
