(Every Python object undergoes a defined lifecycle from allocation to garbage collection: 1. Construction & Initialization \(__init__\):) Tj
T* (When PartyAnimal\("Sally"\) is called, Python performs two actions: - Step A: Calls __new__\(\) to allocate raw memory space for) Tj
T* (the object in RAM. - Step B: Immediately invokes the constructor method __init__\(self, ...\) to initialize instance attributes. 2.) Tj
T* (Active Operation: During this phase, methods are called, state is modified, and the object interacts with other objects. 3.) Tj
T* (Destruction & Deallocation \(__del__\): When an object's reference count drops to zero \(e.g. del s, or the object falls out of) Tj
T* (variable scope\), Python's automatic Garbage Collector deallocates its memory address. Before reclaiming the memory, Python) Tj
T* (optionally calls the destructor method __del__\(self\).) Tj
