(Inheritance allows a new class \(the Child or Subclass\) to inherit attributes and methods from an existing class \(the Parent or) Tj
T* (Superclass\): The Problem Inheritance Solves: Without inheritance, creating specialized classes \(e.g. SavingsAccount and) Tj
T* (CheckingAccount\) requires copying identical logic \(owner verification, balance queries\) into multiple files. Using super\(\) for) Tj
T* (Constructor Delegation: A child class constructor should always call the parent constructor using super\(\).__init__\(...\) to initialize) Tj
T* (shared state: class Account: def __init__\(self, owner, balance\): self.owner = owner self.balance = balance class) Tj
T* (SavingsAccount\(Account\): def __init__\(self, owner, balance, interest_rate=0.03\): super\(\).__init__\(owner, balance\) # Initializes) Tj
T* (parent state self.interest_rate = interest_rate # Adds specialized state) Tj
