0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
42.5196850393700814 320.3151968503935905 Td
(Python supports three distinct method types defined using decorators: 1. Instance Methods: The default method type. Receives) Tj
T* (self as the first parameter. Can access and modify both instance state and class state. 2. Class Methods \(@classmethod\):) Tj
T* (Receives cls \(the class object itself\) as the first parameter instead of self. Cannot access instance attributes. - Primary Use) Tj
T* (Case: Factory constructors \(creating instances from JSON, CSV, or formatted strings\). 3. Static Methods \(@staticmethod\):) Tj
T* (Receives neither self nor cls. Behaves like a plain function placed inside the class namespace for logical grouping. - Primary Use) Tj
T* (Case: Pure utility functions that do not depend on object or class state.) Tj
