(Implement the following 6 comprehensive object-oriented challenges: 1. Inventory Item with Property Validation: Create an) Tj
T* (InventoryItem class with name, unit_price, and quantity_in_stock. Use @property to ensure price > 0 and stock >= 0. Add a total_value) Tj
T* (property. 2. Bank Account Hierarchy with Transaction Auditing: Build an Account base class with deposit and withdraw methods. Create) Tj
T* (a SavingsAccount subclass that enforces a minimum balance of 500, and a CheckingAccount subclass with an overdraft allowance.) Tj
T* (Track transaction timestamps in a list. 3. Vector Mathematics Class with Operator Overloading: Create a Vector2D class representing a) Tj
T* (2D coordinate \(x, y\). Implement __add__, __sub__, __mul__ \(scalar multiplication\), __eq__, and __str__ returning '\(x, y\)'. 4.) Tj
T* (Polymorphic Notification Dispatcher: Create EmailNotifier, SMSNotifier, and SlackNotifier classes sharing a send_alert\(recipient,) Tj
T* (message\) method. Write a broadcast_system_alert\(notifiers, message\) function demonstrating duck typing. 5. Alternative Factory) Tj
T* (Constructor from JSON: Create a CourseModule class with a @classmethod from_json_str\(json_text\) that safely instantiates module) Tj
T* (objects from raw JSON text. 6. Library Catalog Management System: Build a Book class and a LibraryCatalog class. Implement) Tj
T* (__len__, __getitem__, and add/remove book methods supporting lending and availability tracking.) Tj
ET
