(In earlier modules, text parsing required intricate combinations of string methods: find\(\), split\(\), strip\(\), and multi-step slice) Tj
T* (arithmetic. While suitable for simple delimiter separation, real-world data is rarely uniform. Server logs contain varying) Tj
T* (whitespace; user input includes erratic phone number formatting; email addresses have dynamic subdomains; and security) Tj
T* (audits require matching hexadecimal hashes or IPv4 addresses. Solving these complex text patterns using standard procedural) Tj
T* (string methods requires dozens of fragile, nested conditional statements. Regular Expressions \(commonly abbreviated as) Tj
T* ('Regex'\) provide a concise, declarative domain-specific language for searching, validating, extracting, and replacing text patterns.) Tj
T* (Rather than specifying algorithmic step-by-step extraction instructions, you describe the shape and constraints of the target data:) Tj
T* ('find a line starting with From:, followed by whitespace, followed by a sequence of non-whitespace characters containing an @) Tj
T* (symbol.' Based on Chapter 11 of Dr. Charles Severance's 'Python for Everybody' and production Python text-processing) Tj
T* (standards, this module delivers an exhaustive guide to Python's built-in re engine: mastering raw string notation \(r'...'\), character) Tj
T* (classes and meta-characters, greedy versus non-greedy quantifiers, capture groups and named groups, high-performance) Tj
T* (precompiled regex objects \(re.compile\), search-and-replace transformations \(re.sub\), and defensive pattern design to prevent) Tj
T* (catastrophic backtracking.) Tj
ET
