(Consider the task of extracting an email address from an unstructured log line: 'From: stephen.marquard@uct.ac.za Sat Jan 5) Tj
T* (09:14:16 2008' Procedural Approach \(find & slice\): at_pos = line.find\('@'\) space_before = line.rfind\(' ', 0, at_pos\) space_after =) Tj
T* (line.find\(' ', at_pos\) email = line[space_before + 1:space_after] Why Procedural Parsing Breaks: 1. Fragility: If the line contains) Tj
T* (tabs instead of spaces, or leading punctuation, find\(\) selects the wrong boundary indices. 2. Inability to Validate: find\(\) extracts) Tj
T* (whatever text surrounds '@', even if the result is invalid \('@' preceded by spaces or non-email characters\). The Regular) Tj
T* (Expression Approach: import re emails = re.findall\(r'S+@S+', line\) In a single line, re.findall\(\) scans the string, evaluates) Tj
T* (non-whitespace character constraints \(S+\), verifies the presence of '@', and extracts all matches cleanly.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.004 0.2 0.137 rg
42.5196850393700814 173.1970866141734859 Td
(2. The Raw String Notation \(r'...'\) Requirement) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
42.5196850393700814 159.0238582677167187 Td
(In Python string literals, the backslash character \(\) is used as an escape sequence marker: ' ' = newline, ' ' = tab, '' =) Tj
T* (backspace. The Collision Hazard in Regular Expressions: Regex also uses the backslash extensively \(d = digit,  = word) Tj
T* (boundary, s = whitespace\). Without raw strings: To pass the regex pattern  to the re engine, Python string escaping requires '\\b') Tj
T* (so Python passes '' to the regex compiler. If writing complex expressions, you end up needing '\\\\' to match a single literal) Tj
T* (backslash! The Solution: Raw Strings \(r'...'\) Prefixing a string with 'r' tells the Python interpreter to treat backslashes as literal) Tj
T* (characters without interpreting escape sequences: pattern = r'[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+.[A-Z|a-z]{2,}' Rule of Thumb:) Tj
T* (ALWAYS declare regular expression patterns using raw string notation r'...'.) Tj
ET
