(In complex regular expressions containing 5 or more capture groups, accessing matches by numeric index \(group\(1\), group\(2\)\)) Tj
T* (becomes fragile and unreadable. Syntax: \(?P<name>pattern\) Python allows assigning explicit semantic identifiers to capture) Tj
T* (groups: log_pattern = r'\(?P<ip>d{1,3}\(?:.d{1,3}\){3}\) - [\(?P<timestamp>[^]]+\)] "\(?P<method>[A-Z]+\) \(?P<endpoint>[^ ]+\)) Tj
T* (HTTP/d.d" \(?P<status>d{3}\)' Match Dictionary Access: match = re.search\(log_pattern, log_line\) if match: data =) Tj
T* (match.groupdict\(\) print\(data['ip']\) # '192.168.1.1' print\(data['endpoint']\) # '/api/v1/courses' print\(data['status']\) # '200') Tj
