(Implement the following 6 comprehensive regular expression challenges: 1. Strict Email Validator & Component Extractor: Write a) Tj
T* (function validate_and_parse_email\(email_str\) that returns a dictionary with 'username', 'domain', and 'tld' if the email is strictly valid, or) Tj
T* (None if invalid. 2. Comprehensive Phone Number Normalizer: Given raw phone inputs in various formats \('\(555\) 123-4567',) Tj
T* ('555.123.4567', '5551234567', '+1 555-123-4567'\), normalize all valid 10-digit numbers into standard '\(555\) 123-4567' format using) Tj
T* (re.sub\(\). 3. Web Log IP and Response Status Aggregator: Stream through Apache-style log lines, extract the client IP address and) Tj
T* (HTTP status code using named groups, and return the count of 200 \(OK\) vs 404 \(Not Found\) responses. 4. Markdown Link Extractor:) Tj
T* (Extract all Markdown hyperlinks in the format [Link Text]\(https://target.url\) from a markdown document, returning a list of tuples: \(text,) Tj
T* (url\). 5. Password Complexity Policy Validator: Validate passwords ensuring they meet security rules: at least 8 characters, at least 1) Tj
T* (uppercase letter, at least 1 lowercase letter, at least 1 number, and at least 1 special character \(@#$%^&*\). 6. Code Comment Stripper:) Tj
T* (Write a function that strips all Python single-line comments \(# ...\) from code lines while preserving string literals containing '#' characters.) Tj
ET
