/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
42.5196850393700814 649.4175590551180903 Td
(In traditional standalone computing, software operates strictly within the confines of local memory and local disk drives.) Tj
T* (However, the true power of modern programming emerges when Python reaches across the global Internet to communicate with) Tj
T* (remote servers, retrieve real-time data feeds, automate browser workflows, and harvest knowledge from unstructured web) Tj
T* (pages. To write networked Python programs, you must understand the underlying communication architecture: the Transport) Tj
T* (Control Protocol \(TCP\) and Internet Protocol \(IP\). A network connection is established across a 'Socket' - a two-way) Tj
T* (communication channel between two programs running across the network, uniquely identified by an IP address and a Port) Tj
T* (number. Atop TCP sockets runs the World Wide Web's foundational application protocol: the HyperText Transfer Protocol) Tj
T* (\(HTTP\). Based on Chapter 12 of Dr. Charles Severance's 'Python for Everybody' and enterprise web scraping engineering) Tj
T* (standards, this module bridges the gap between low-level network mechanics and high-level data harvesting: constructing raw) Tj
T* (socket connections to send manual HTTP GET commands, utilizing Python's urllib module to treat global URLs as simple file) Tj
T* (streams, respecting web scraping ethics and robots.txt protocols, mastering the BeautifulSoup \(bs4\) HTML parser to navigate) Tj
T* (complex DOM trees, following hyperlink trails programmatically, and downloading binary media assets via chunked network) Tj
T* (streams.) Tj
ET
