(Python's socket module provides direct C-level access to the operating system's networking stack: Workflow of a Socket Client:) Tj
T* (1. Create Socket: s = socket.socket\(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM\) - AF_INET: Specifies IPv4 addressing. -) Tj
T* (SOCK_STREAM: Specifies reliable, stream-oriented TCP. 2. Connect to Remote Host: s.connect\(\('data.pr4e.org', 80\)\) 3. Send) Tj
T* (Encoded Bytes: Sockets transmit raw bytes, not Python strings! You must encode text: s.sendall\(cmd.encode\('utf-8'\)\) 4. Receive) Tj
T* (Loop: Read chunks of data into a local buffer: while True: data = s.recv\(512\) # Reads up to 512 bytes if len\(data\) < 1: break #) Tj
T* (EOF: Server closed connection print\(data.decode\('utf-8'\), end=''\) 5. Close Socket: s.close\(\)) Tj
ET
