42.5196850393700814 255.9687401574805108 Td
(To understand web services, compare how applications interact across the web: 1. Web Scraping \(HTML\): HTML is designed for) Tj
T* (presentation to human eyes \(fonts, layouts, colors, responsive wrappers\). - Problem: Fragile. When a marketing team updates a) Tj
T* (website's layout, classes change and scrapers crash. - Inefficiency: The server spends bandwidth and compute sending) Tj
T* (megabytes of CSS, images, and HTML styling when the client only wants a single price number. 2. Web Services \(REST / JSON) Tj
T* (/ XML\): A Web Service exposes structured programmatic endpoints \(APIs\) designed strictly for consumption by software code. -) Tj
T* (Resilience: The data contract \(schema\) remains stable even if the company's marketing website changes completely. - Compact:) Tj
T* (Transmits raw semantic data payloads \(JSON or XML\) with minimal network overhead.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.004 0.2 0.137 rg
42.5196850393700814 161.2915748031497287 Td
(2. XML vs. JSON: Head-to-Head Comparative Architecture) Tj
ET
