(Python's standard library includes ElementTree, a fast hierarchical XML parser: Sample XML: <person> <name>Dr. Ananya) Tj
T* (Sharma</name> <phone type="intl">+91 98765 43210</phone> <email hide="yes"/> </person> Parsing Workflow: import) Tj
T* (xml.etree.ElementTree as ET # Step 1: Parse XML string into Element tree root = ET.fromstring\(xml_data\) # Step 2: Query child) Tj
T* (tags using find\(\) print\(root.find\('name'\).text\) # 'Dr. Ananya Sharma' # Step 3: Extract tag attributes using get\(\)) Tj
T* (print\(root.find\('phone'\).get\('type'\)\) # 'intl' print\(root.find\('email'\).get\('hide'\)\) # 'yes' Searching Multiple Children with findall\(\): users =) Tj
T* (root.findall\('user'\) # Returns list of Element objects) Tj
ET
