(JSON maps directly onto Python's native data structures: Python <-> JSON Type Mapping Table: - Python dict <-> JSON Object) Tj
T* (\({...}\) - Python list/tuple <-> JSON Array \([...]\) - Python str <-> JSON String \("..."\) - Python int/float <-> JSON Number \(42, 3.14\) -) Tj
T* (Python True / False <-> JSON true / false - Python None <-> JSON null The 4 Core JSON Functions: 1. json.loads\(str\): Load) Tj
T* (from String -> Parses JSON text into a Python dict/list. 2. json.dumps\(obj\): Dump to String -> Serializes a Python dict/list into a) Tj
T* (JSON string. 3. json.load\(file\): Load from File -> Reads JSON directly from an open file handle. 4. json.dump\(obj, file\): Dump to) Tj
T* (File -> Writes Python data to an open file in JSON format.) Tj
ET
