(7. API Authentication Standards: API Keys & Bearer Tokens) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
42.5196850393700814 116.220708661417234 Td
(Most production APIs require client authentication: 1. Query Parameter Authentication \(Simpler APIs\):) Tj
T* (https://api.weather.com/v1/forecast?city=Bengaluru&apikey=secret_key_123 2. HTTP Authorization Header \(Industry Standard\):) Tj
T* (Sending tokens inside HTTP headers keeps sensitive credentials out of server access logs and browser histories: Authorization:) Tj
T* (Bearer <jwt_or_oauth_token> In Python: req = urllib.request.Request\(api_url\) req.add_header\('Authorization', f'Bearer) Tj
T* ({api_token}'\) req.add_header\('Accept', 'application/json'\) with urllib.request.urlopen\(req\) as resp: ...) Tj
ET
