(To query normalized data across multiple tables, use the SQL JOIN clause: Syntax: SELECT Track.title, Album.title, Artist.name) Tj
T* (FROM Track JOIN Album ON Track.album_id = Album.id JOIN Artist ON Album.artist_id = Artist.id WHERE Artist.name =) Tj
T* ('AC/DC' Types of Joins: 1. INNER JOIN \(Default\): Returns rows only where there is an exact match in both joined tables. 2.) Tj
T* (LEFT OUTER JOIN: Returns ALL rows from the left table, even if no corresponding row exists in the right table \(unmatched) Tj
T* (columns are filled with NULL\).) Tj
