(Consider modeling Course Enrollment: - A Student can enroll in Many Courses. - A Course can have Many Students. This) Tj
T* (Many-to-Many relationship cannot be represented with a single Foreign Key. The Solution: A Junction \(Membership\) Table: 1.) Tj
T* (User Table: id \(PK\), name, email 2. Course Table: id \(PK\), title 3. Member Table: user_id \(FK\), course_id \(FK\), role \(0=Student,) Tj
T* (1=Instructor\), PRIMARY KEY \(user_id, course_id\) Querying Many-to-Many: SELECT User.name, Course.title, Member.role) Tj
T* (FROM User JOIN Member ON User.id = Member.user_id JOIN Course ON Member.course_id = Course.id) Tj
ET
